     "<div dir=\"ltr\">Hi All,<div><br></div><div>I am looking for references to understand the use of modindices, so I look up pdf doc,</div><div><br></div><div>&quot;<a href=\"https://users.ugent.be/~yrosseel/lavaan/multiplegroup6Dec2012.pdf\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://users.ugent.be/~yrosseel/lavaan/multiplegroup6Dec2012.pdf&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792421987801000&amp;usg=AOvVaw2fgH4YpV87CaUUrhPKyjcT\">https://users.ugent.be/~yrosseel/lavaan/multiplegroup6Dec2012.pdf</a>&quot;<br></div><div><br></div><div>I try to follow and run the R codes printed on  p. 26 of the pdf,</div><div><br></div><div>model3 &lt;- cfa(HS.model, data=HolzingerSwineford1939,\r\ngroup=&quot;school&quot;, group.equal=c(&quot;loadings&quot;,&quot;intercepts&quot;)) </div><div>modindices(model3)</div><div><br></div><div>It seems that I cannot find the print out of &quot;modindices(model3)&quot; which shows item 3 and item 7 have intercept\r\nestimates that are non-invariant across groups.</div><div><br></div><div>Instead, my print out of the results is shown</div><div><br></div><div><div>       lhs op rhs block group level     mi    epc <a href=\"http://sepc.lv\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://sepc.lv&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792421987801000&amp;usg=AOvVaw2m8erHZbICduVZThQAEMF6\">sepc.lv</a> sepc.all sepc.nox</div><div>1    visual =~  x1     1     1     1  2.955  0.446   0.398    0.342    0.342</div><div>4   textual =~  x4     1     1     1  0.003 -0.006  -0.006   -0.005   -0.005</div><div>7     speed =~  x7     1     1     1  0.011 -0.027  -0.015   -0.014   -0.014</div><div>37   visual =~  x1     2     2     1  2.955 -0.446  -0.375   -0.321   -0.321</div><div>40  textual =~  x4     2     2     1  0.003  0.006   0.006    0.005    0.005</div><div>43    speed =~  x7     2     2     1  0.011  0.027   0.019    0.018    0.018</div><div>88 