     2,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0;margin-left:0.8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><div>I look up pdf doc,</div><div><br></div><div>&quot;<a href=\"https://users.ugent.be/~yrosseel/lavaan/multiplegroup6Dec2012.pdf\" rel=\"nofollow\" target=\"_blank\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://users.ugent.be/~yrosseel/lavaan/multiplegroup6Dec2012.pdf&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792421987802000&amp;usg=AOvVaw2elnwLIwV7StCZIc1-imCi\">https://users.ugent.be/~yrosseel/lavaan/multiplegroup6Dec2012.pdf</a>&quot;</div></div></blockquote><div><br></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div>That is an outdated document.  You cannot obtain modification indices for estimated parameters using<font face=\"courier new, monospace\"> modindices() </font>anymore (for several years now). </div><div> </div><div>You can obtain them for equality-constrained parameters from the more general score-test function:</div><div><br></div><div><div style=\"background-color:rgb(250,250,250);border-color:rgb(187,187,187);border-style:solid;border-width:1px\"><code><div><span style=\"color:#000\">lavTestScore</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">model3</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span></div></code></div><br></div><div>To see which parameters the printed parameter labels refer to, see your parameter table:</div><div><br></div><div><div style=\"background-color:rgb(250,250,250);border-color:rgb(187,187,187);border-style:solid;border-width:1px\"><code><div><span style=\"color:#000\">parTable</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">model3</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span></div></code></div><div><br></div>You will notice the score tests are not identical to the old document, but the same 2 indicators are flagged for having unequal intercepts.</div><div><br><div><div>Terrence D. Jorgensen</div><div>Assistant Professor, Methods and Statistics</div><div>Research Institute for Child Development and Education, the University of Amsterdam</div><div><a href=\"http://www.uva.nl/profile/t.d.jorgensen\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://www.uva.nl/profile/t.d.jorgensen&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792421987802000&amp;usg=AOvVaw2JIGn8YqGA0oluq5EXrXQ_\">http://www.uva.nl/profile/t.d.jorgensen</a></div></div><div></div></div><div><br></div></div>"
    ]
